WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.069
-We don't always have enough
time to cover

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.871
everything in the news,
so here with a recap

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.439
is one of our writers,
Amber Ruffin,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.608
in a segment we call,
"Amber Says What."

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.844
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:15.481
-You guys,
things have been crazy!

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:19.285
Okay, so, first of all,
the Super Bowl was this weekend.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:23.456
And I saw the halftime show
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.659
Shakira played the drums,
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.629
Then J.Lo did some
crazy stuff on a pole,

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.765
and I was like, "What?"

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:36.236
Then someone reminded me
that J.Lo is 50,

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:41.240
and I was like,
"What kind of sorcery is this?"

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.144
Who are you?
Jen-jamin Buttons?"

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.981
Then I found out part of Trump's
border wall fell over,

00:00:48.981 --> 00:00:51.885
and I was like, "What?"

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.888
And then I found out
it fell over onto Mexico,

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.424
and I was like, "Oh, what?!"

00:00:58.424 --> 00:01:02.228
What did this? A bulldozer?
A wrecking ball?

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.963
No, the wind.

00:01:04.963 --> 00:01:06.365
The wind blew it over.

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:09.168
And I was like, "What?"

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.104
Well, at least that
won't happen again,

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.940
because if there's one thing
that's super-rare

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.976
on planet Earth, it's wind.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.745
P.S., of course the wall
got blown down.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:25.084
The only thing propping
it up was racism.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:29.823
[ Laughs ] Oh!

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:32.258
If you think about it,
yeah, that was...

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:36.796
Then, the National Science
Foundation's solar telescope

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.764
took its first picture
of the sun.

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:41.867
And I saw it
and was like, "What?"

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:43.268
From far away, the sun is

00:01:43.268 --> 00:01:46.105
a beautiful hot ball of
glowing gases whose gravity

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:47.973
holds the solar system together.

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:53.679
But up close, the sun ain't
nothing but a big, old ashy leg.

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:55.347
Hey, astronauts, the next time

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:58.584
you go up there,
bring some lotion.

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:01.987
Then Beyoncé came out
with a new line of clothes.

00:02:01.987 --> 00:02:03.856
And I was like, "What?!"

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:08.261
Then she sent her famous friends
giant boxes of the clothes.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.663
And I was like, "What?!
That is so cool."

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:14.033
Hey, Seth, did you get a big old
box of clothes from Beyoncé?

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.969
-I think you know I did not.

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:20.073
-So then, soon after,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:22.775
people started noticing how
the line of clothing

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:25.612
resembled uniforms at Popeyes.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.146
And I looked at the similarities

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:31.183
and I was like,
"What...a coincidence!"

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:34.386
Then Popeyes came out with
its own line of clothing

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:37.022
that looks a lot like
Beyoncé's fashion line.

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:40.059
And I was like, "What?!"

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.829
Popeyes!

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.798
I'm a size medium.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.934
Then presidential candidate
Michael Bloomberg

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.471
met a dog for what I guess
was the first time,

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:56.976
and this happened.

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.711
I was like, "What?!

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:03.216
Did this billionaire just try to
shake a dog's mouth?"

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:06.251
Have you never met a dog before?

00:03:06.251 --> 00:03:10.923
Man, dogs are for petting.
Booties are for shaking.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:13.726
Then a zoo in England
recently discovered

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.862
that their big cats
are more active

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.697
in their environment
if you spray

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:20.332
Calvin Klein's
Obsession for Men.

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:22.435
And I was like, "What?!"

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:26.338
That's not a surprise.
That cologne is from 1998.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.173
Of course cougars love it.

00:03:28.173 --> 00:03:31.377
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]
Y'all have to stop.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:34.947
You can't just be
"ohh-ing" everything.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.750
"Cougars? Ohh!

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.519
Racism? Ohh!"

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:43.856
Then I read an article that said
Harry and Meghan's choice

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.525
to step back from
the royal family

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:48.961
was a missed opportunity to heal
race relations in the U.K.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.164
And I was like, "What?!"

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:54.533
It is not her job to fix
your [bleep] country.

00:03:54.533 --> 00:03:56.569
Besides, she already taught you

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.671
the most valuable
lesson of all --

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.573
black people don't have time
for your [bleep]

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:02.808
so treat us right
or we'll move to Canada!

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:07.580
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.550
I said, we will move to Canada!
Do you hear me, Seth?

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:14.954
-Sorry. What?
-That's what I thought!

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:19.158
Then something happened that you
are never going to believe.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:21.427
Okay, for real, last week,

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.930
in a town called
Perryville, Maryland,

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:27.166
a white man robbed a bank
in blackface.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:31.236
And I was like,
"What are you doing?!"

00:04:31.236 --> 00:04:33.406
Now, you know there's probably
only one black person

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:38.144
in Perryville, Maryland,
and his life is bad enough.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.179
But, on the bright side,
that bank robber

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.480
probably got home,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:49.321
and his wife was like, "Ooh!
No, Bob. Leave it on."

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:53.292
Then, yeah, they had weird sex.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:57.497
Then I heard my favorite person
to look at, Billy Porter,

00:04:57.497 --> 00:05:00.232
was at the Grammys,
and I was like,

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:02.301
"What...did he wear?"

00:05:02.301 --> 00:05:05.171
And I saw him,
and he looked beautiful.

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:09.608
Then I saw that he had a crazy
hat, and I was like, "What?!

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.110
It's gorgeous!"

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.579
Then I saw that it had an
internal mechanism

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.681
that opened and shut its
bedazzled veil,

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:18.017
and I was like, "What?!"

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.553
Look.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:24.357
Man, I tell you what -- if I
ever got my hands on that hat,

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:26.692
we wouldn't be doing no
"Amber Says What."

00:05:26.692 --> 00:05:30.229
We'd be doing "Billy Porter's
Hat Says What."

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:33.999
And guess what.
I did. And now we are.

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:36.269
It's time for "Billy Porter's
Hat Says What."

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:40.272
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:43.876
You guys,
things have been crazy.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:46.512
First of all, I heard that
Gwyneth Paltrow

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:49.582
is selling a candle
that smells like her vagina.

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:52.985
And I was like...

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:58.223
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:58.223 --> 00:06:01.527
Then Trump's campaign held
a rally to win over

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:04.930
black voters by handing out cash
in a black community.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:09.968
And I was like...

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:12.171
"Where you doing that at?"

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:16.175
But then I found out the Black
Women's Caucus of South Carolina

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:19.212
endorsed Tom Steyer
for president.

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:22.314
And when I realized the closest
thing the Democratic Party

00:06:22.314 --> 00:06:29.955
has to a black woman is
Tom Steyer, I was like...

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:34.260
This Has been "Amber Says What
in Billy Porter's Hat."

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.895
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

